      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bd570eedbe1156cf5eb1c7e|full_name}: And what does it with this feature request?\n\nIt's no joke with more stablized face cam, i know because deaf people use shaking to express yes or no (by nodding) but since VRChat is mostly designed for hearing people so they speak.\n\nMuted, deaf and bad hearing nods pretty much and for some viewers is bit too much shaking view. The shaking can more reduced for viewers for more pleasuring view with requested feature.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-11T14:01:41.865Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's good your stream camera has stabilized option to keep camera view nicely for viewers, to make it for example less sick.\n\nBut i saw the face camera (the main camera actually) is not stabilized. Especially if you use face to give many and big nods to others or dance pretty hard so your face camera will shake pretty much. That makes it unpretty to watch for viewers. \n\nSo it should good idea to add option in the menu for stabilized face camera. I know there is small problem: it must not stabilized for yourself or you will bit sick because projected picture doesn't match VR view position.\n\nStabilized face cam is more for streaming purposes. So VRChat show stabilized cam only on desktop window, but VR video feed should untouched and unstabilized to prevent disorientation yourself, aka direct feed.\n\nShould this possible?",
